cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use USB Gym, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "USB Gym: A Gymnasium Testbed for Closed-Loop Ultrasound View Matching"
version: 2.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23942190
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/tohnperfect/USBGym"
url: "https://github.com/tohnperfect/USBGym"
abstract: >-
  USB Gym is a CT-based Gymnasium testbed for closed-loop ultrasound probe view matching. For any
  probe pose over a patient's labeled CT it renders a B-mode frame and resolves probe-skin contact in
  MuJoCo; an agent moves the probe to reproduce a target view of the same patient. Renderer, texture
  stage, mask source, controller, reward and anatomy source are plug slots with small interfaces, and
  an oracle ladder of privileged and image-only controllers locates the remaining pose error.
keywords:
  - ultrasound
  - simulation
  - reinforcement learning
  - gymnasium
  - view matching
  - robotic ultrasound
  - medical imaging
